# `scripts/sql/` is bind-mounted into the `postgres-init` container of the
# OptimCE dev stack and executed there by `psql`. This repo is developed on
# Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which would hand the container CRLF files —
# and a stray \r turns into a syntax error whose message points nowhere near the
# cause. The monorepo pins its own provisioning SQL the same way, but git
# attributes are per-repository and do not follow into a submodule, so the rule
# has to be repeated here.
scripts/sql/**/*.sql  text eol=lf
scripts/**/*.sh       text eol=lf

# The `run:` blocks in these workflows are shell scripts executed on a Linux
# runner. A stray \r from a Windows checkout is the same failure one directory
# over, with the error attributed to whatever line happens to be last.
.github/workflows/*.yml  text eol=lf
